ng":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Yum! Brands, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, develops, operates, and franchises traditional and non-traditional quick service restaurants in the United States, China, and internationally. The company operates in four segments: KFC Division, Taco Bell Division, Pizza Hut Division, and Habit Burger & Grill Division. It also operates restaurants under the KFC, Pizza Hut, Taco Bell, and Habit Burger & Grill brands, which specialize in chicken, Mexican-style food and pizza categories, made-to-order chargrilled burgers, sandwiches, and other products. The company was formerly known as TRICON Global Restaurants, Inc. and changed its name to Yum! Brands, Inc. in May 2002. Yum! Brands, Inc. was incorporated in 1997 and is headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher Lee Turner | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 49K people. Revenue per employee of $168K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 18\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Yum! Brands, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $43.3B market cap on $8.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and -5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 70% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 63-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $1.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.29\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 4.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Carries a 63% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6335549105888962},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 24% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Yum China Doubles Restaurant Count To 20K+ In Just 6 Years","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/opinion/26/11/63246918/yum-china-doubles-restaurant-count-to-20k-in-just-6-years","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794584691.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Yum! Brands, Inc. Declares Quarterly Dividend of $0.75 Per Share","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/yum-brands-inc-declares-quarterly-133000100.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794576600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.61,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"What Does KFC's Reported Switch to Coca-Cola Mean for Yum! Brands?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/what-does-kfcs-reported-switch-to-coca-cola-mean-for-yum-brands","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794316620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.524,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Weekly Investment Analysts\u2019 Ratings Changes for Yum! Brands (YUM)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/weekly-investment-analysts-ratings-changes-for-yum-brands-yum.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794250605.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.354,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Yum! Brands (YUM) Posts Strong Q3 Growth, Is The 10% Undervaluation Still There?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-yum/yum-brands/news/yum-brands-yum-posts-strong-q3-growth-is-the-10-undervaluati","